  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme Management Support for the Just Transition Water Security programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This component will provide support for programme management to oversee delivery of each of the programme&#x2019;s component and to coordinate the programme in country.  FCDO will deploy programme funded positions, most likely based within the office of one of the delivery partners for other components.  The staff will focus on engaging national stakeholders to support the programme&#x2019;s objectives on water governance and wider delivery. 
Up to five programme funded posts may be required and be recruited wherever two or more delivery components are operational. The needs will be assessed during programme delivery. ECED would locate programme funded positions where greater support is required to ensure the programme delivers on HMG in-country priorities. 
There is also a need for the FCDO to build close relationships with key stakeholders, particularly partner governments to support programme delivery.  Post will be established in accordance with HMG policy for country-based staff whose will be time limited.  No contract will be offered that runs longer than the duration of the whole programme. Decision on programme funded posts will be taken based on the need for additional support, the value of a dedicated FCDO staff member in country and wider programme management implications.
These in-country facilitators or coordinators will coordinate country-based delivery plans, support stakeholder dialogues and any negotiations and policy dialogue, ensure programme coherence and supervise work on the ground.  Permissions will follow rules laid on in relevant ProF Guide. The facilitators will report to a line manager in the FCDO country office in the first instance and to the SRO and PRO on broader policy matters and grant management.  The facilitators will participate in monthly OCU and PESC steering meetings.    
Arrangements to share costs with other relevant FCDO programmes, as well as regional facilitators will be explored.</narrative>
  </description>
